# @react-three/fiber v9 declares Expo / React Native packages as OPTIONAL peer
# dependencies. npm 7+ tries to resolve them anyway and fails against React 19
# with an ERESOLVE conflict on react-dom. Legacy peer handling skips peer
# resolution entirely, which is what we want: the web renderer needs none of
# the Expo stack, and none of it is installed.
#
# Trade-off accepted 22 September 2026: npm no longer enforces peer ranges for
# any package in this repo. Check peer warnings by hand when upgrading Prisma,
# NextAuth or React.
legacy-peer-deps=true
